            <ArticleTitle>[The diagnosis of abdominal tuberculosis in military medical and prophylactic institutions].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>48-51, 96</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Abdominal tuberculosis constitutes 0.5-2% in the general structure of the disease, nevertheless it requires special methods of treatment. The authors draw the rules of diagnosis at the early stages of the disease development on the base of 55 patients' case records. They also present a list the most important research projects on chronic and acute abdominal cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
